node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store
# RUNTIME state, not content. The store rewrites these on every edit, so tracking them shows a
# diff whenever anyone uses the app; on Cloud Run this directory is a mounted bucket. The shipped
# corpus lives in examples/ (tracked) and is copied here on first boot.
diagrams/*.json
diagrams/*.json.tmp
secrets/
google-credentials.json
google-token.json
# H9.29: a connection code is a bearer credential and the plaintext exists once. A file holding
# one sat untracked in this directory, which is one `git add -A` away from being published --
# and this repository's own commit flow is exactly that. Ignored by NAME rather than trusting
# anyone to remember, and the safer habit is to keep it outside the working tree entirely.
code.txt
*.code.txt
codes.json
cli/.draw_context
.claude/

# The draw lineage clones (`draw` 2021, `graph` 2023, `prism` 2026) are a local research checkout,
# referenced by docs as provenance and never committed. Ignored by name so a clone made for
# reference cannot be published by a `git add -A`, which is the same habit H9.29 guarded above.
.refs/

# How THIS instance is deployed: the procedure, the project and bucket identifiers, the DNS and
# certificate ordering, the pages served outside IAP, and a probe that runs against a real bucket.
# Kept in the working tree because the operator needs it, ignored because the repository describes
# the system rather than one hosting of it -- `docs/spec/HOSTING.md` carries the reasoning that
# survives the choice.
#
# UNTRACKED MEANS UNBACKED. Nothing here is in git history after the commit that removed it, so a
# fresh clone has no deploy/ and a wipe of this working tree loses it. It belongs somewhere durable
# outside this repository; the copy here is a convenience, not the record.
deploy/

